------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 RIPKit for PCBoard:  Updating from v1.11 to v1.20
==============================================================================

Only a few steps are necessary for to upgrade to v1.20 of the RIPKit from
version 1.11.

   1)  Make sure you are running v15.21 of PCBoard or higher

   2)  Unzip RIPKIT.ZIP to the \PCB\RIP subdirectory using the -n switch.
       If the RIP files are stored in C:\PCB\RIP\, perform these steps:

           CD\TEMP (where you may have unzipped RIPKT120.ZIP)
           PKUNZIP -n -o RIPKIT.ZIP C:\PCB\RIP\

   3)  Unzip the CMDFILES.ZIP file to the directory where your command
       display files are stored.  See PCBSetup | File Locations | System
       Files if you are unsure.

   4)  Copy the PCBTEXT.RIP file in the \PCB\RIP\ subdirectory to the
       directory where the PCBTEXT files are stored for your system.
       PCBSetup | File Locations | System Files will tell you the location
       if you are unsure.

       Once you have copied the file, make sure the size of your PCBTEXT.RIP
       is 59,120 bytes.  That is the size of the file for use with v15.2.


*** NOTE:  Read HISTORY.TXT if you want a detailed listing of what has been
***        updated.
